{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport sys\nimport itertools\n\ndef solve():\n    data = sys.stdin.buffer.read().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    n = int(data[0])\n    a1, a2, a3 = int(data[1]), int(data[2]), int(data[3])\n    b1, b2, b3 = int(data[4]), int(data[5]), int(data[6])\n    mx = min(a1, b2) + min(a2, b3) + min(a3, b1)\n    temp = 0\n    perms = list(itertools.permutations([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]))\n    for per in perms:\n        ta1, ta2, ta3 = a1, a2, a3\n        tb1, tb2, tb3 = b1, b2, b3\n        tmx = 0\n        for el in per:\n            if el == 1:\n                t1 = min(ta1, tb1)\n                ta1 -= t1; tb1 -= t1; tmx += t1\n            elif el == 2:\n                t1 = min(ta1, tb3)\n                ta1 -= t1; tb3 -= t1; tmx += t1\n            elif el == 3:\n                t1 = min(ta2, tb2)\n                ta2 -= t1; tb2 -= t1; tmx += t1\n            elif el == 4:\n                t1 = min(ta2, tb1)\n                tb1 -= t1; ta2 -= t1; tmx += t1\n            elif el == 5:\n                t1 = min(ta3, tb3)\n                ta3 -= t1; tb3 -= t1; tmx += t1\n            elif el == 6:\n                t1 = min(ta3, tb2)\n                tb2 -= t1; ta3 -= t1; tmx += t1\n        temp = max(temp, tmx)\n    sys.stdout.write(f\"{n - temp} {mx}\\n\")\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    solve()\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 1.0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        solve();\n    }\n\n    static void solve() {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        List<Integer> list = new ArrayList<>();\n        while (sc.hasNextInt()) {\n            list.add(sc.nextInt());\n        }\n        if (list.isEmpty()) {\n            return;\n        }\n        int n = list.get(0);\n        int a1 = list.get(1);\n        int a2 = list.get(2);\n        int a3 = list.get(3);\n        int b1 = list.get(4);\n        int b2 = list.get(5);\n        int b3 = list.get(6);\n\n        int mx = Math.min(a1, b2) + Math.min(a2, b3) + Math.min(a3, b1);\n\n        List<int[]> perms = new ArrayList<>();\n        int[] initial = {1,2,3,4,5,6};\n        permute(initial, 0, perms);\n\n        int temp = 0;\n        for (int[] perm : perms) {\n            int ta1 = a1, ta2 = a2, ta3 = a3;\n            int tb1 = b1, tb2 = b2, tb3 = b3;\n            int tmx = 0;\n            for (int el : perm) {\n                int t1;\n                switch (el) {\n                    case 1:\n                        t1 = Math.min(ta1, tb1);\n                        ta1 -= t1; tb1 -= t1; tmx += t1;\n                        break;\n                    case 2:\n                        t1 = Math.min(ta1, tb3);\n                        ta1 -= t1; tb3 -= t1; tmx += t1;\n                        break;\n                    case 3:\n                        t1 = Math.min(ta2, tb2);\n                        ta2 -= t1; tb2 -= t1; tmx += t1;\n                        break;\n                    case 4:\n                        t1 = Math.min(ta2, tb1);\n                        tb1 -= t1; ta2 -= t1; tmx += t1;\n                        break;\n                    case 5:\n                        t1 = Math.min(ta3, tb3);\n                        ta3 -= t1; tb3 -= t1; tmx += t1;\n                        break;\n                    case 6:\n                        t1 = Math.min(ta3, tb2);\n                        tb2 -= t1; ta3 -= t1; tmx += t1;\n                        break;\n                }\n            }\n            temp = Math.max(temp, tmx);\n        }\n\n        System.out.println((n - temp) + \" \" + mx);\n    }\n\n    static void permute(int[] arr, int k, List<int[]> list) {\n        if (k == arr.length) {\n            list.add(arr.clone());\n            return;\n        }\n        for (int i = k; i < arr.length; i++) {\n            swap(arr, k, i);\n            permute(arr, k + 1, list);\n            swap(arr, k, i);\n        }\n    }\n\n    static void swap(int[] arr, int i, int j) {\n        int tmp = arr[i];\n        arr[i] = arr[j];\n        arr[j] = tmp;\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.99\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -3.731181277544238e-05, -3.2186455882765586e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -7.486063259420916e-05, -0.06330690532922745, -9.858122211880982e-05, 0.0, -0.001292465953156352, -0.0019330164650455117, -0.00016223068814724684, -0.002685870509594679, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -5.709961988031864e-05, -4.768370445162873e-07, -9.536738616588991e-07, 0.0, -4.768370445162873e-07, -1.7523612768854946e-05, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -0.007301432080566883, -4.768370445162873e-07, -1.2040065485052764e-05, -0.048587895929813385, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.016381533816456795, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -0.00142020417843014, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -0.0001401803019689396, -0.0007114263135008514, 0.0, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.2993727978027891e-05, -2.622600959512056e-0